VOTECHAIN LOCAL DEMO - WINDOWS POWERSHELL
==========================================

Requirements
------------
- Windows 10/11
- Node.js 20.9+ and npm
- Git (only needed to clone)
- Docker Desktop with Docker Compose, OR a local PostgreSQL server and database
- Ports 3000, 5433, and 8545 available

FIRST-TIME SETUP FROM GITHUB
----------------------------
Run these commands in PowerShell:

  git clone https://github.com/testacc307070-cloud/VoteChain.git
  cd VoteChain
  npm ci
  Copy-Item .env.example .env

npm ci installs packages and generates the Prisma Client.

START THE DATABASE
------------------
Recommended: install and start Docker Desktop, then run from the project folder:

  docker compose up -d --wait postgres

This starts PostgreSQL on 127.0.0.1:5433. The local demo database is named
votechain; its Compose-only development user/password are configured in
.env.example. Do not use these development credentials outside a local demo.

If using a local PostgreSQL installation instead, create a database and user,
then change DATABASE_URL in your ignored .env file to match that local server.
Keep the database running while VoteChain is open.

START GANACHE (SECOND POWERSHELL WINDOW)
----------------------------------------
Open another PowerShell window, change to the VoteChain project folder, and run:

  npm run blockchain:node

Leave this window open. Ganache is the local test blockchain; it does not connect
to or deploy anything online.

DEPLOY THE CONTRACT AND PREPARE THE DATABASE
--------------------------------------------
In the first PowerShell window, from the VoteChain project folder, run:

  npm run blockchain:deploy

Copy the printed contract address. Open .env and replace the value of
VOTECHAIN_CONTRACT_ADDRESS with that address. This deployment address belongs
to the current Ganache session; deploy again if you restart Ganache with a fresh
chain.

Then run:

  npx prisma migrate deploy
  npm run db:seed

START THE WEB APP
-----------------
In the first PowerShell window, run:

  npm run dev

Wait for Next.js to report it is ready, then open:

  http://localhost:3000

Keep the database, Ganache, and web app running in their respective windows.
To stop the web app or Ganache, press Ctrl+C in that service's window. Stop the
Compose database with this command (its data volume is preserved):

  docker compose down

